id: pm-llbnua
title: Sentry-injected release artifacts exceed the CI package budget because pre- and post-injection packlists share one ceiling
description: "Release run 33882558951 passed the 20,000,000-byte package budget before publication only until Sentry injected debug IDs into the shipped JavaScript. The exact v2026.9.4 artifact then measured 20,140,358 bytes and failed, while a clean pre-injection exact-tag build measures 19,926,990 bytes. Model and gate both artifact phases explicitly so CI constrains the base package, release constrains the actual Sentry-injected package, and immutable exact-tag recovery can publish without moving the tag or weakening source-map observability."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: distribution,packaging,release,sentry
created_at: "2026-09-04T14:42:11.523Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-04T16:01:54.644Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-04T16:01:54.084Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-04T16:01:54.084Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "CI and release enforce named, reviewable pre-injection and post-injection artifact budgets; the post-injection gate validates the bytes actually published without disabling Sentry debug IDs; negative controls reject an unknown profile and oversize artifacts in either profile; workflow contracts prove the base gate runs before injection and the injected gate runs after it; exact v2026.9.4 recovery passes packaging, npm/npx/bunx and installed-agent acceptance, and GitHub Release verification without moving the immutable tag.; Sentry upload and release finalization occur only after the Sentry-injected artifact gate passes, so a rejected package causes no external observability side effect.; Manual recovery acceptance proves reviewed controls remain outside the immutable tagged working tree and both artifact profiles execute through the preserved path."
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make package-size assurance represent the exact artifact users install
value: The release must preserve Sentry symbolication and artifact-size discipline without a false mismatch between CI and publication environments.
why_now: Immutable v2026.9.4 is unpublished and release recovery is blocked before npm publication.
parent: pm-e70zh5
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: GitHub Actions Release exact-tag recovery for v2026.9.4 after Sentry debug-ID injection
repro_steps: "Build immutable v2026.9.4 and npm pack: 19,926,990 bytes; inject Sentry debug IDs into dist and rerun scripts/release/package-artifact-gate.mjs: hosted run reports 20,140,358 > 20,000,000."
resolution: "Added named dual-phase artifact budgets; fail-closed profile parsing and finite numeric validation; base, injection, post-injection gate, then Sentry side-effect ordering; and runner-temporary preservation of the reviewed gate and budget before an exact-tag checkout, without modifying the package tree."
expected_result: "Normal and recovery releases enforce current reviewed artifact policy over the exact publishable package, reject malformed or oversized artifacts before external observability effects, preserve immutable tag contents, and permit v2026.9.4 publication with Sentry debug IDs."
actual_result: "Focused tests pass 29/29, full coverage is exact 100/100/100/100 over 603 files and 8,364 tests, direct tracker-aware static quality passes, and isolated v2026.9.4 recovery accepts 19,926,977-byte base and 20,140,345-byte injected artifacts while SHA-256 proving tagged controls unchanged."
affected_version: 2026.9.4
component: release-packaging
regression: true
customer_impact: "Validated SDK and CLI changes cannot reach npm, npx, bunx, or GitHub Release."
